 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "s1_p01",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "We're doing backprop on exercise sheet 4. Can you explain what backpropagation actually computes? I get that it's the gradient but not why it goes backwards.",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:02:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p02",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "For a 2-layer MLP with sigmoid hidden units I wrote dL/dW1 = dL/dy * W2 * x. Is that missing something?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:04:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p03",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "how does the chain rule work on a computational graph when one node feeds into two others?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:06:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p04",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Why do people use ReLU instead of sigmoid in hidden layers?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:08:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p05",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "I computed the gradient of the loss wrt the bias in layer 1 as the sum of the deltas over the batch. Is summing right or should it be the mean?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:10:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p06",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "what is the derivative of tanh? I think it's 1 - tanh^2 but I'm not sure why",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:12:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p07",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "In the computational graph for f = (x+y)*z, what are the local gradients at each node?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:14:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p08",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Our network trains fine with 3 layers but with 10 layers the loss barely moves. Is that the vanishing gradient problem?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:16:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p09",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "What's the derivative of softmax combined with cross-entropy? The sheet says it simplifies to y_hat - y",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:18:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p10",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Leaky ReLU vs ReLU, does the small negative slope really matter in practice?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:20:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p11",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Should I use SGD or Adam for the exercise? The sheet doesn't say.",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:22:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p12",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Why exactly does the gradient shrink layer by layer with sigmoid? Is it because the derivative is at most 0.25?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:24:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p13",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "How do I do gradient checking with finite differences? What epsilon should I pick?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:26:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p14",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "My gradient check gives a relative error of 1e-3. Is that good enough or is my backward pass wrong?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:28:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p15",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Does ReLU fix vanishing gradients completely, or can it still happen?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:30:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p16",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "What does momentum do in SGD, intuitively?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:32:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p17",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "When I backprop through a max pooling layer, where does the gradient go?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:34:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p18",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Do residual connections help with vanishing gradients? How?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:36:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p19",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "My learning rate of 0.1 makes the loss explode and 0.001 is super slow. How do people choose the learning rate?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:38:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p20",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "What's the bias correction in Adam for? I don't get why the first steps are biased.",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:40:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p21",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Xavier vs He initialization, which one goes with ReLU and why?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:42:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p22",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Why can't we just initialize all weights to zero?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:44:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p23",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "How does dropout work at test time? Do I scale the weights?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:46:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p24",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Is L2 regularization the same as weight decay?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:48:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p25",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "In the backward pass of batch norm, why does the gradient have three terms?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:50:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p26",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "I keep confusing myself: in the chain rule for vectors, when do I transpose the Jacobian?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:52:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p27",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Is gradient clipping the fix for exploding gradients, like the opposite of the vanishing problem?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:54:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p28",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "I derived dL/dz for softmax + cross-entropy and got y_hat - y, but only for a single example. How does it look for a batch?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:56:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p29",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "learning rate schedules: is cosine decay better than step decay?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:58:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_p30",
   "conversationId": "s1_focused:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Can you quiz me on backprop? Give me a small network and I'll compute the gradients myself.",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T10:00:00Z"
  }
 ]
